; Room records (rooms 0-105)
;
; Layout (see rooms.py, which decodes it the way the code reads it): byte 0
; flags; +1..+6 up to three word slots naming the room - noun first, its top
; nibble the article (1 'a', 2 'an', 8 none); +7/+8 the room's own description
; message (0 = none); then exits, 3 bytes each - direction (the verb number
; 1-10), the thing in the way (0 = nothing) and the destination room - ended by
; $FF.
; .
; The thing in the way is what the room description names: "To the east there
; is a deep stream" comes from an exit whose 'door' is the stream. An exit with
; destination 0 is only ever scenery: the exit finder #R$D448 skips it, so it
; is described but never offered as a visible exit and can't be taken.
; .
; Confirmed by play: all 206 exits were tried (tools/walkall.py); 194 move the
; player to the decoded destination, and the other 12 are exactly the ones the
; code says must refuse - 7 scenery exits with destination 0, and 5 through a
; passage narrower than the player (see the move pre-check at #R$DCD2).
b$84E1 DEFB $04,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00 ; {Room 0 (room 0): flags $04, name
 $84E9 DEFB $00                             ; words (no name), no description
                                            ; of its own}
 $84EA DEFB $FF                             ; Room 0 exits: no exits
