; Entity records: every person, object and door
;
; Layout (from the code that reads it, see objects.py): byte 0 = n, the number
; of location bytes; +1 = id of the thing containing this one ($FF = none) -
; the link that TAKE, SIT IN and GET OUT all change; +2 = size (capacity, for a
; container); +4 bits 0-2 = can hold things; +5 bit 5 = open; +7 onwards = up
; to four two-byte word slots (noun, then adjectives); +15 onwards = the n
; rooms this thing is in (a door lists every room it connects); then the
; thing's own (verb, shared action) list, ended by $FF.
; .
; Checked against play: the player (0) is 'you' in room 8, Watson (3) is inside
; his armchair (24), the oil lamp (22) is in room 8, the Daily Chronicle (25)
; is inside Watson - which is why READ CHRONICLE says there is none to examine
; - and 'your money' (27) is carried by the player, as INVENTORY reports.
