; The actor table: who acts, and where each is in its plan script
;
; 24 eight-byte records, ended by $FF, walked once per turn. +0 the actor's
; thing id; +1/+2 its position in its plan script (see #R$CC78); +3 the plan's
; verb, +4/+5 the plan's direct and indirect objects ($FF = none; loaded by
; #R$D008, saved by #R$D026); +6/+7 the minute (counted like #R$9FDD from the
; start) at which the actor next acts, set by the main loop (#R$A064); 0 at the
; start, so everyone acts in the first minute. #R$CC0E finds a record by id.
; The seven steam trains and two cabbies are actors too.
; .
; CORRECTED: earlier rounds read +1/+2 as a handler address; it is a script
; position, and it changes as the actor's script runs.
