; Action record: Lestrade finds the large rock in the stream (RUN at $E0A2)
;
; Addresses named in the title: #R$E0A2.
; .
; The extra step of EXAMINE CLOSELY DEEP STREAM. If the player is in room 88
; (the east side of the stream) on Tuesday, the large rock (indirect object,
; thing 93) is made visible (+5 and +6 bit 7), put in the player's room and
; held by Inspector Lestrade (the direct object): 'As you search the river
; Lestrade comes over to help. He stumbles and slid...' (#R$7B5A). Seen: thing
; 93 +5 went from $20 to $A0 and +6 from 0 to $80.
; .
; Seen in the emulator (9 November, tools/experiments/record_coverage.py over
; the 15 stored routes): the body ran 10 times in 10 of them, run by you. Every
; one of its 17 instructions was executed (tools/experiments/insn_coverage.py).
;
;  Input:$A034 The direct object
;        $A015 The indirect object's record
; Output:F NZ; the rock revealed in room 88 on Tuesday
c$E0AD DEFB $4D,$07,$1C,$E0 ; Action record header: flags $4D; bit 6: pre-check
                            ; at #R$E01C; byte 1 $07
 $E0B1 LD A,($A00A)         ; Read the current actor's room (#R$A00A) into A -
                            ; Player in room 88 (east side)?
 $E0B4 CP $58               ; Compare A with $58
 $E0B6 JR NZ,$E0DD          ; No: nothing happens (#R$E0DD)
 $E0B8 LD A,($9FE1)         ; Read the day (#R$9FE1) into A - Day 1 (Tuesday)?
 $E0BB CP $01               ; Compare A with $01
 $E0BD JR NZ,$E0DD          ; If A differs from $01, skip ahead to #R$E0DD
 $E0BF LD IX,($A015)        ; IX = the indirect object's record
                            ; (#R$A012($A015))
 $E0C3 SET 7,(IX+$06)       ; Set bit 7 of byte +6 of the record at IX - Mark
                            ; it as seen and visible (+6 and +5 bit 7)
 $E0C7 SET 7,(IX+$05)       ; Set bit 7 of byte +5 of the record at IX
 $E0CB LD A,($A00A)         ; Read the current actor's room (#R$A00A) into A -
                            ; Move it into the player's room (+15)
 $E0CE LD (IX+$0F),A        ; Store A in byte +15 of the record at IX
 $E0D1 LD A,($A034)         ; Read #R$A032($A034) in "Game variables" into A -
                            ; And make the direct object its holder (+1)
 $E0D4 LD (IX+$01),A        ; Store A in byte +1 of the record at IX
 $E0D7 LD HL,$7B5A          ; Point HL at the message "AS YOU SEARCH THE RIVER
                            ; LESTRADE COMES OVER TO... (#R$7B5A) - Print the
                            ; message #R$7B5A
 $E0DA CALL $A59F           ; Call the routine "Print the message at HL"
                            ; (#R$A59F)
*$E0DD OR $01               ; Make A non-zero, which clears the zero flag, and
                            ; hand that back to the caller - Return NZ
 $E0DF RET                  ; Return to the caller

