; Action record: the first messenger takes a note from Basil (RUN at $EE95)
;
; Addresses named in the title: #R$EE95.
; .
; Prints 'A messenger arrives at the door, takes a note from Basil and
; dissapears down the street.' (#R$75E8). It is run by Phipps's script at
; #R$EE95 on Tuesday at 1pm, only when you (or the china man) are in Camden
; Street or Basil's front yard (rooms 32 and 102). No stored route is there at
; that hour, so I tested it on 9 November (tools/experiments/untraced_tests.py,
; part E): I replayed the winning route to Tuesday 12:30pm in Kings Cross Road,
; moved the player to Camden Street by writing the room number into memory (the
; only poke in this pass) and typed WAIT: at about 1:00pm the message was
; printed. Its sibling at #R$EFAC (Wednesday 9:50am) ran in the stored routes.
; .
; Every one of its 6 instructions was executed
; (tools/experiments/insn_coverage.py plus the targeted tests described above).
;
; Output:F NZ; the message printed
c$EF9C DEFB $00,$00  ; Action record header: flags $00; byte 1 $00
 $EF9E LD HL,$75E8   ; Point HL at the message text, "A messenger arrives at
                     ; the door, takes a note from Basil and disappears down
                     ; the street." (#R$75E8)
; This entry point is used by the routine at #R$EFAC.
*$EFA1 LD A,$01      ; A = 1: the value the output switch needs for the message
                     ; to appear on screen. (A second entry point: the sibling
                     ; record at #R$EFAC joins here with its own HL.)
 $EFA3 LD ($5C3C),A  ; Store it in the output-switch byte
                     ; (#LINK(rom_symbols#a5C3C)($5C3C)), so the print routine
                     ; really draws the text instead of staying silent
 $EFA6 CALL $A59F    ; Print the message at HL (#R$A59F)
 $EFA9 OR $01        ; OR $01 makes A non-zero, which clears the zero flag: the
                     ; plan interpreter reads "not zero" as "the action
                     ; happened"
 $EFAB RET           ; Return to the plan interpreter

; Action record: the second messenger gives a note to Basil (RUN at $EF01)
;
; Addresses named in the title: #R$EF01.
; .
; Prints 'A messenger arrives at the door, gives a note to Basil and dissapears
; down the street.' (#R$7603), with the same output switch setting as #R$EF9C.
; Run by Phipps's script at #R$EF01 on Wednesday morning when you or the china
; man are outside, which is why it appears in the winning route.
; .
; Seen in the emulator (9 November, tools/experiments/record_coverage.py over
; the 15 stored routes): the body ran 7 times in 7 of them, run by phipps.
; Every one of its 2 instructions was executed
; (tools/experiments/insn_coverage.py).
;
; Output:F NZ; the message printed
c$EFAC DEFB $00,$00  ; Action record header: flags $00; byte 1 $00
 $EFAE LD HL,$7603   ; Point HL at the message "A MESSENGER ARRIVES AT THE
                     ; DOOR, GIVES A NOTE TO... (#R$7603)
 $EFB1 JR $EFA1      ; Go back to #R$EFA1

; Action record: Phipps goes to sleep (RUN at $EE3D, $EEBB)
;
; Addresses named in the title: #R$EE3D, #R$EEBB.
; .
; Sets the actor's state word to SLEEPING ($07F0), the high nibble of +8 to 1,
; and clears bit 6 of +5 (not a person any more), through #R$F1C1. Seen: thing
; 6 (Phipps) +9/+10 went from 0 to $07F0, +8 from $86 to $16 and +5 from $E0 to
; $A0.
; .
; Seen in the emulator (9 November, tools/experiments/record_coverage.py over
; the 15 stored routes): the body ran 22 times in 12 of them, run by phipps.
; Every one of its 7 instructions was executed
; (tools/experiments/insn_coverage.py).
;
;  Input:$A036 The actor
; Output:F NZ; the actor asleep, no longer a person to talk to
c$EFB3 DEFB $00,$00   ; Action record header: flags $00; byte 1 $00
 $EFB5 LD DE,$07F0    ; Load DE with $07F0 - DE = $07F0, B = $10
 $EFB8 LD B,$10       ; Load B with $10
; This entry point is used by the routine at #R$EFC7.
*$EFBA LD A,($A036)   ; Read #R$A032($A036) in "Game variables" into A - The
                      ; actor's record (#R$F1C1)
 $EFBD CALL $F1C1     ; Call the routine "Set a thing's state word and state
                      ; bits" (#R$F1C1)
 $EFC0 RES 6,(IX+$05) ; Clear bit 6 of +5
 $EFC4 OR $01         ; Make A non-zero, which clears the zero flag, and hand
                      ; that back to the caller - Return NZ
 $EFC6 RET            ; Return to the caller

; Action record: Phipps wakes at 7 - or shoots you if you are in the house (RUN
; at $EE46, $EEC3, $EEDB, $EF09)
;
; Addresses named in the title: #R$EE46, #R$EEC3, #R$EEDB, #R$EF09.
; .
; If the player is in one of the rooms of Basil's house (33 to 39, the seven
; compares at #R$EFC9-#R$EFE4) control goes to #R$DFCC and Basil shoots you;
; otherwise the state word is cleared, the high nibble of +8 becomes 8 and bit
; 6 of +5 is set again - he is awake and a person again. Seen: thing 6 +9/+10
; went from $07F0 to 0, +8 from $16 to $86 and +5 from $A0 to $E0 (11 sampled
; runs); with you in the house the branch to #R$DFCC ran twice in the stored
; routes.
; .
; Seen in the emulator (9 November, tools/experiments/record_coverage.py over
; the 15 stored routes): the body ran 5,592 times in 11 of them, run by phipps.
; Every one of its 20 instructions was executed
; (tools/experiments/insn_coverage.py).
;
;  Input:$A009 The player's room
; Output:F NZ; Phipps wakes, or shoots the player if the player is in Basil's
; .        house
c$EFC7 DEFB $00,$00   ; Action record header: flags $00; byte 1 $00
 $EFC9 LD A,($A009)   ; Read the room the player is in, which decides what is
                      ; shown (#R$A002($A009)) into A - The player's room
                      ; (#R$A002($A009)): one of Basil's house (33 entrance
                      ; hall to 39 yard; the seven compares run $23, $21, $22,
                      ; $26, $25, $24, $27)?
 $EFCC CP $23         ; Compare A with $23
 $EFCE JR Z,$EFE6     ; If A equals $23, skip ahead to #R$EFE6
 $EFD0 CP $21         ; Compare A with $21
 $EFD2 JR Z,$EFE6     ; If A equals $21, skip ahead to #R$EFE6
 $EFD4 CP $22         ; Compare A with $22
 $EFD6 JR Z,$EFE6     ; If A equals $22, skip ahead to #R$EFE6
 $EFD8 CP $26         ; Compare A with $26
 $EFDA JR Z,$EFE6     ; If A equals $26, skip ahead to #R$EFE6
 $EFDC CP $25         ; Compare A with $25
 $EFDE JR Z,$EFE6     ; If A equals $25, skip ahead to #R$EFE6
 $EFE0 CP $24         ; Compare A with $24
 $EFE2 JR Z,$EFE6     ; If A equals $24, skip ahead to #R$EFE6
 $EFE4 CP $27         ; Compare A with $27
*$EFE6 JP Z,$DFCC     ; Yes: take the other branch at #R$DFCC
 $EFE9 LD DE,$0000    ; Load DE with $0000 - No: DE = 0, B = $80, and clear
                      ; then re-set bit 6 of the record's +5 (#R$EFBA)...
 $EFEC LD B,$80       ; Load B with $80
 $EFEE CALL $EFBA     ; Call #R$EFBA (inside "Action record: Phipps goes to
                      ; sleep (RUN at...")
 $EFF1 SET 6,(IX+$05) ; Set bit 6 of byte +5 of the record at IX - ...so it
                      ; ends with bit 6 set again: awake and a person (the
                      ; state word and the +8 nibble were cleared by AWAIT 6
                      ; phipps [fail: wait here] DO 128 PUT: self, room 103
                      ; (old mill DO 136 IS HOUR 15 [fail: wait here] RUN
                      ; #R$E52F START COUNTDOWN of (dobj) DO 131 IS IN: 0 you,
                      ; room 103 (old PASS RUN #R$E57A TICK the countdown PASS
                      ; AWAIT 4 chief constable straker RUN #R$F198 CHANCE:
                      ; succeed if a PRINT message #R$7552: "YOU SEEMS AT GOTO
                      ; #R$F017 PASS RUN #R$F198 CHANCE: succeed if a PRINT
                      ; message #R$7552: "YOU SEEMS AT RUN #R$F198 CHANCE:
                      ; succeed if a RUN #R$F198 CHANCE: succeed if a DO 135 GO
                      ; THROUGH DOOR: -, - DO 131 IS IN: self, room 63 (browns
                      ; DO 135 GO THROUGH DOOR: 45 large oak GOTO #R$F029 DO 40
                      ; SIT IN [busy; ok #R$F029] DO 25 GET OUT OF [busy] GOTO
                      ; #R$F029 Entry (not reached from anywhere GOTO #R$F05C
                      ; AWAIT 2 inspector lestrade [busy; DO 128 PUT: self,
                      ; room 92 (jones SAY TO 11 local police man message PASS
                      ; AWAIT 2 inspector lestrade [busy; SAY TO 2 inspector
                      ; lestrade message SIGNAL 2 inspector lestrade [busy] DO
                      ; 134 FOLLOW UNTIL IN: 2 inspector PRINT message #R$6CB9:
