; Plan script: the German agent (actor 104) - Phipps's buyer
;
; Entry points: #R$EFF6 = german agent (actor 104).
; .
; Decoded by tools/plan.py; see #R$CC78 for the language. Each sub-block is one
; instruction. Room and object numbers are as the game uses them (the reference
; pages list both). Labels for verbs 128-140 and for the common helper records
; (#R$E52F, #R$E57A, #R$E588, #R$E5A8, #R$DDBE, #R$F198) were read from those
; records' code, not tried one by one in the emulator.
; .
; In an instruction, 'plan dobj' and 'plan iobj' are not fixed objects: they
; mean the direct and indirect object currently held in the actor's plan
; registers (bytes +4 and +5 of its actor record), so the same step works on
; whatever the actor is dealing with - for the player, the objects of the
; command just typed. 'plan verb' is the verb register (+3), 'self' is the
; acting character, and '-' means none.
; .
; He waits for Phipps's signal (AWAIT), is put at Old Mill Road (room 103), and
; from 3pm counts down like Phipps; if you turn up there (#R$F009: IS IN you,
; room 103) he joins Phipps's own flight code at #R$EF4A - put in Main Street,
; the 4:55 to London, Kings Cross Road, a cab to Buckingham Palace Road and on
; to platform one at Victoria, where he too runs the last scene (#R$9E48) if he
; finds you there. In the winning run (see #R$E7E7) he was already standing on
; platform one at Victoria when the train came in at 6:40 - 'You can see a
; german agent.' - and Basil walked in two minutes later. Read from the script;
; the sighting is from the emulator.
b$EFF6 DEFB $19,$06,$F6,$EF             ; AWAIT 6 phipps [fail: wait here]
 $EFFA DEFB $42,$80,$FB,$67             ; DO 128 #R$E497(PUT): self, room 103
                                        ; (old mill road) [busy]
