; Action record: reveal the burning note (RUN at $EF0C)
;
; Addresses named in the title: #R$EF0C.
; .
; Sets bit 7 of the direct object's +5 - the bit #R$C821 tests for being
; visible. Run by Phipps's script at #R$EF0C on Wednesday morning with the
; burning note (thing 85) as the object; seen: +5 went from $20 to $A0, which
; is the note appearing in the bedroom at 10:05am.
; .
; Seen in the emulator (9 November, tools/experiments/record_coverage.py over
; the 15 stored routes): the body ran 9 times in 9 of them, run by phipps.
; Every one of its 4 instructions was executed
; (tools/experiments/insn_coverage.py).
;
;  Input:$A013 The direct object's record
; Output:F NZ; the object visible (+5 bit 7 set)
c$F1F6 DEFB $07,$00   ; Action record header: flags $07; byte 1 $00
 $F1F8 LD IX,($A013)  ; Read #R$A012($A013) in "Game variables" into IX - Set
                      ; bit 7 of the direct object's +5 (the bit #R$C821 tests
                      ; for visibility)
 $F1FC SET 7,(IX+$05) ; Set bit 7 of byte +5 of the record at IX
 $F200 OR $01         ; Make A non-zero, which clears the zero flag, and hand
                      ; that back to the caller - Succeed
 $F202 RET            ; Return to the caller

; Verb 133 (scripts only): clear bit 0 of a thing's +5 flags
